## 5.0 Quality Objectives
- Validate Jira API authentication and permissions before attempting requirement extraction.
- Ensure robust error handling for 401 Unauthorized and related authentication failures.

## 6.0 Test Schedule / Milestone
- Test design: 2 days (1 QA automation engineer)
- Environment setup: 1 day (DevOps support)
- Script development: 2 days (QA automation engineer)
- Execution & reporting: 2 days (QA automation engineer)
- Total duration: 1 week

## 7.0 Resource Estimate
- 1 QA automation engineer (5 days)
- 0.5 DevOps engineer (1 day)

## 8.0 Entry/Exit Criteria
<Entry and exit criteria for each test phase.>

## 9.0 Risk Mitigation Table
| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation Action | Owner |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| R1 | Jira API authentication failures due to expired/misconfigured credentials | High | Medium | Implement credential rotation and alerting; use mock services for test isolation | QA Lead |
| R2 | Test environment instability (mock service downtime) | Medium | Medium | Monitor mock service health, auto-restart scripts, fallback to local stubs | DevOps |
| R3 | Incomplete negative test coverage for error codes | Medium | Low | Review all error handling paths, automate 401/403/500 scenarios | QA Engineer |
| R4 | Timeline slippage due to resource contention | Medium | Medium | Pre-allocate QA/DevOps resources, daily standups for blockers | Project Manager |
| R5 | Tool integration issues (e.g., Playwright/OWASP ZAP conflicts) | Low | Low | Isolate tool runs, validate toolchain compatibility in CI | QA Lead |

